WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
It's kind of unimaginable
not believing in them.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.320
My grandmother had
an elf friend in a rock.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.600
The elves come to me in my dreams.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.520
I'm convinced elves do exist.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.880
I'm professor of Folkloristics
at the University of Iceland.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.320
One of the areas of research
that I've been working on

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.320
is so-called 'elves' or 'álfar',

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.000
along with 'huldufólk',
'the hidden ones',

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.840
that Icelanders are so interested in.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.080
I can picture some kind
of idea of a hidden person,

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:36.400
kind of looks like a human.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.600
They have a little bit
old-fashioned clothing.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.080
They have their own society here,
emotions and feelings.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.880
They are born, grow old, and die.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.200
I think they live in rocks.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.880
They can show themselves
if they choose to, but rarely do.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.720
But you never know
when it will happen.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.320
You have maybe 10%
say that they don’t believe,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.560
and then those that do believe
is again about 10%.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:10.480
But in between you have all of the
rest, who are 'maybe', 'possibly',

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.120
'probably', 'who knows'.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.520
INTERVIEWER: So if I asked
you then if you think literally

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:15.800
that they exist?

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.600
We can't say no.
Yeah, you can't say no.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:18.720
They will come haunt us.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.640
It's not that they believe,

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.640
they are worried that there
might be something there

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.760
when it comes down to it,
that you're not going to mess with.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.360
My name is Pétur Matthíasson

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.840
and I'm Head of Communication with
the Icelandic Road Administration.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.000
So this is the rock that we moved,
from the place where the road is,

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.640
and we moved it over here.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.760
People thought that this
might be an elf church,

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:53.440
and these people asked us
if we could maybe move the rock.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.280
We will look into it. Not because
we believe so much in elves

00:01:58.360 --> 00:01:59.760
at the Road Administration,

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.800
we look at is as part
of our cultural inheritance.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:13.600
We know that people in the Viking
times were buried in mounds

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:15.240
which showed above the earth.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.200
As each generation goes by,

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.720
the living memory of the people
within the ground,

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.600
turns into a much more hazy idea,

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.920
about beings that live out of sight.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.920
The nature of Iceland makes
you feel really strong emotions.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.600
A nation where your house can be
destroyed by something you can't see.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.360
We naturally try to explain
these things by means of

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.320
personifying the environment.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.800
And everyone is surrounded by nature,
you see the mountains,

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.400
you see the ocean, everywhere.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.760
The belief started because of this
strong connection that we still have.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:57.600
I think there is a pressure
from the society as a whole,

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.880
that we are the people
who believe in elves

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.840
and we should tell everybody that.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.280
Because we have been trying
to get more tourists for a long time.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.880
I think a lot of people
will say they believe in elves,

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:09.320
but in heart, they don't.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.720
If we couldn't have moved it,
we would have smashed it down.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.440
It's just a rock.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.600
Whether you believe it or not,
these stories about the elves

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.040
and these creatures,
they teach us to respect nature.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.840
And the elves here are,

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.440
for the most part I think, respected.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.920
Should the law consider
the huldufólk?

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.160
Maybe not, but I think maybe
the law should try to consider

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.720
what rights the nature can have,

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.920
because it doesn't
really have a voice.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.600
Even though it's quite outdated,

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:54.160
maybe the huldufólk
is giving nature a voice.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.080
There are people coming
from countries

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:00.400
who've in a sense lost this
connection, this magic.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.760
In Iceland you can talk about
the elves and these other worlds

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.400
to everybody and people
will not lock you up.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.480
It makes Iceland different
and they like being different

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.520
to other nations, in all ways.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:13.840
We want it to be like this.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.080
It would be a nicer place to live
if there were hidden people there.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.120
Don 't you think?

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:28.760
Thanks for watching. 
Don’t forget to subscribe! :)

